KernelSU vendoring/configuration checks
=====================================

Run from the kernel root:

    python3 tools/testing/selftests/kernelsu/test_integration.py
    python3 tools/testing/selftests/kernelsu/test_integration.py --config out/.config

Checks all 104 imported source files against recorded upstream Git blob IDs or
reviewed local SHA-256 overrides, licenses, regular files/no nested .git, the
single Kbuild/Kconfig inclusion, clean-build header wiring, opt-in default, and
miatoll's resolved built-in hook/security policy. No network or compiler needed.

For a separate output configuration with CONFIG_KSU disabled:

    python3 tools/testing/selftests/kernelsu/test_integration.py \
        --config /path/to/disabled/.config --expect-disabled

CI calls the enabled check after olddefconfig if the selected defconfig requests
CONFIG_KSU=y. An unintended dropped dependency/hook option stops the build.

These are integrity/integration checks, NOT runtime tests of root authorization,
SELinux policy changes, syscall hooks, safe mode or compatibility. A full build
and device boot with a known-good recovery path are still required.

The current source manifest also records the corrected SUSFS 2.3.0 overlay on
this same backslashxx revision. After the FinaSU overlay, 15 files have reviewed overrides; 89 match
upstream blobs. See Documentation/filesystems/susfs/ for bridge provenance and
additional source/configuration/host tests. KSU-only CONFIG_KSU_SUSFS=n remains
supported; the KSU test does not require SUSFS to be enabled.

FinaSU alternative-manager checks
--------------------------------

    python3 tools/testing/selftests/kernelsu/test_finasu.py
    python3 tools/testing/selftests/kernelsu/test_finasu.py \
        --host-tests --negative-tests --cc clang
    python3 tools/testing/selftests/kernelsu/test_finasu.py \
        --host-tests --cc 'clang -fsanitize=undefined -fno-sanitize-recover=all'

Checks six pinned postimages, package/UID/cache sequencing, real kernel identity,
read-only display ABIs/permissions. Host tests extract production package/key
selection, identity accessors, crown/scanner and metadata handlers into
finasu_model.c, mocking certificate-parser results, VFS and credentials. Runs
four configured-hook branches, output-boundary/fault tests and optionally six
deliberate regressions. Not APK signature, concurrent VFS, Android or boot tests.

CI calls the FinaSU source check alongside the KSU check. See
Documentation/dev-tools/finasu-manager.md for signing policy, single-active-manager
behavior, commands, provenance chaining with SUSFS and runtime limitations.
